1
00:00:01,340 --> 00:00:04,160
Hi. I'm Malcolm Stewart.

2
00:00:04,160 --> 00:00:05,510
John Marchetta.

3
00:00:05,510 --> 00:00:09,130
Sit down, sit down.

4
00:00:09,130 --> 00:00:11,890
Susan has told me a great deal about you.

5
00:00:11,890 --> 00:00:13,720
She says you're quite a man.

6
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:14,240
She says

7
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:17,900
a lot of wonderful things about you too, Mr. Stewart.

8
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:20,380
That's always nice to hear, Mr. Marchetta.

9
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:21,420
Call me John.

10
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:23,980
May I call you Malcolm?

11
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:25,850
Let's talk business.

12
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:27,840
That's music to my ears.

13
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:28,550
I understand

14
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:30,790
you used to be in the construction business.

15
00:00:30,790 --> 00:00:33,860
Yup. Forty-three years.

16
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:35,610
Here's a brief description

17
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:42,040
of forty-three years of on-the-job training.

18
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:44,770
That is some history!

19
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:46,760
You're a valuable asset, Malcolm.

20
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,590
Very valuable.

21
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:50,740
Thank you.

22
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:54,540
Yup. Forty-three years.

23
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:57,010
Half that time in my own construction company.

24
00:00:57,010 --> 00:01:00,810
Big jobs--factories, shopping malls.

25
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:02,670
That kind of thing.

26
00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:04,130
Then you retired.

27
00:01:04,130 --> 00:01:05,790
Yes.

28
00:01:05,790 --> 00:01:07,760
After my wife died,

29
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:09,670
and I felt I should spend more time

30
00:01:09,670 --> 00:01:12,820
with my children and grandchildren.

31
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:14,320
I lived in Florida,

32
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:15,920
and they lived in New York.

33
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:16,730
I understand.

34
00:01:16,730 --> 00:01:19,070
My dautghter Cami lives in New York.

35
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:21,840
I like being near her.

36
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:22,870
When I came here,

37
00:01:22,870 --> 00:01:25,920
I planned to take a few months off.

38
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:30,240
Relax with the family and then look for some work.

39
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:33,050
Put my experience on the line ...

40
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:34,460
but, unfortunately,

41
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:37,730
there isn't any work for a retired person my age.

42
00:01:37,730 --> 00:01:38,490
Sometimes there is,

43
00:01:38,490 --> 00:01:40,750
and sometimes there isn't.

44
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:42,830
Well, I'm involved with an organization,

45
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:46,250
and we're trying to resolve that problem.

46
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:47,590
What's that?

47
00:01:47,590 --> 00:01:49,010
TOPS.

48
00:01:49,010 --> 00:01:55,160
T-O-P-S--means Talented Older People's Society.

49
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:57,050
I'd like to be a member.

50
00:01:57,050 --> 00:01:58,280
How much are the dues?

51
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:00,920
There are no dues.

52
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:04,270
The organization serves major companies in this city.

53
00:02:04,270 --> 00:02:05,800
Why?

54
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:08,170
Because our members are men and women like you.

55
00:02:08,170 --> 00:02:12,320
Experienced, talented, retired.

56
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:14,260
But our members want to go out there

57
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:15,660
and use their talents.

58
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:18,220
They want to work.

59
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:20,300
That is fantastic, John!

60
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:24,220
I've got an idea for you, Malcolm.

61
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:25,700
Just fill out this form for me.

62
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,310
It'll only take a few minutes.

63
00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:28,290
Sit right here,

64
00:02:28,290 --> 00:02:30,300
and do it while I talk to my secretary.

65
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:33,900
When I get back, we'll talk about my new factory.

66
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:35,540
My company is a member of TOPS.

67
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:39,320
So I try hard to find opportunities for people like you.

68
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:40,660
Malcolm.

69
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:42,030
And when I see an opportunity,

70
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:44,060
I can act on it.

71
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:50,140
Well, I can use your brainpower on the job right now.

72
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:51,190
Have you got time this morning

73
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:53,750
to go over to the construction site with me?

74
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:55,690
I'd like to have you meet my foreman--

75
00:02:55,690 --> 00:02:57,690
get some background on the job.

76
00:02:57,690 --> 00:02:59,940
I've got plenty of time.

77
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:01,440
I'll be right back.

78
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:21,120
We'll go over to the job site together.

79
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:25,420
Malcolm, you worked on the Spaceport project?

80
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:28,570
My company was the contractor.

81
00:03:28,570 --> 00:03:30,810
I built the theater there

82
00:03:30,810 --> 00:03:32,640
with my own two hands, practically.

83
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:33,540
I understand.

84
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:33,910
Well,

85
00:03:33,910 --> 00:03:36,970
I'm glad to see you two guys getting along so well

86
00:03:36,970 --> 00:03:38,330
because, Danny,

87
00:03:38,330 --> 00:03:39,460
Malcolm is on the TOPS team.

88
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:41,990
He's going to be working with you for a while.

89
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:44,960
His experience will be valuable to both of us.

90
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:46,710
Welcome aboard, Malcolm!

91
00:03:46,710 --> 00:03:48,150
I'm going back to my office.

92
00:03:48,150 --> 00:03:49,570
Give me a call later, Malcolm.

93
00:03:49,570 --> 00:03:52,640
I'll tell you the time and date of the next TOPS meeting.

94
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:53,850
I'd like you to meet the group.

95
00:03:53,850 --> 00:03:55,030
I will, John.

96
00:03:55,030 --> 00:03:56,800
And again--thanks.

97
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:59,080
No ... thank you.

98
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:03,230
And thank Susan.

99
00:04:03,230 --> 00:04:04,870
He's quite a man.

100
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:08,220
A real inspiration for me.

101
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:10,380
[04:07.02]OK, Danny.

102
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:10,900
I know you didn't expect to have me around,

103
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:13,510
but I think I can be of some help to you.

104
00:04:13,510 --> 00:04:14,930
Let me tell you something, Malcolm.

105
00:04:14,930 --> 00:04:16,130
With your background and experience,

106
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:17,380
I can learn something

107
00:04:17,380 --> 00:04:19,580
... and I do need some advice on a difficult problem.

108
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:24,580
Let me show you this.

109
00:04:24,580 --> 00:04:28,290
I don't want to give you a final opinion

110
00:04:28,290 --> 00:04:31,940
without studying these building plans more carefully.

111
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:35,580
But a simple solution might be

112
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:37,430
to move the air-conditioning units

113
00:04:37,430 --> 00:04:40,430
instead of redesigning the entire system.

114
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:44,710
It might be simpler and less expensive .

115
00:04:44,710 --> 00:04:47,790
You just earned your weight in gold, Malcolm.

116
00:04:47,790 --> 00:04:52,690
Welcome aboard!

117
00:04:52,690 --> 00:04:54,720
It all happened so quickly!

118
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:56,460
I can't believe it!

119
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:58,870
I'm glad Mr. Marchetta was so helpful.

120
00:04:58,870 --> 00:05:00,290
He was more than helpful.

121
00:05:00,290 --> 00:05:03,630
He actually took me to meet his foreman.

122
00:05:03,630 --> 00:05:06,250
I'm thrilled for you, Grandpa.

123
00:05:06,250 --> 00:05:09,350
I don't know how to thank you, Susan.

124
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:11,670
You're a wonderful granddaughter.

125
00:05:11,670 --> 00:05:13,690
It's good to see you so happy.

126
00:05:13,690 --> 00:05:16,250
I'll be at the construction site tomorrow.

127
00:05:16,250 --> 00:05:17,780
What are you doing tomorrow night?

128
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:18,730
I'm not doing anything.

129
00:05:18,730 --> 00:05:20,170
Why?

130
00:05:20,170 --> 00:05:22,110
How about a date with your grandfather?

131
00:05:22,110 --> 00:05:25,100
I owe you a good steak dinner.

132
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:26,730
I'll accept.

133
00:05:26,730 --> 00:05:27,660
Tomorrow night.

134
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:29,430
You and me. Dinner.

135
00:05:29,430 --> 00:05:31,000
What time?

136
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,890
I'll pick you up here at seven .

137
00:05:32,890 --> 00:05:34,190
Is that OK?

138
00:05:34,190 --> 00:05:35,390
I can't wait!

139
00:05:35,390 --> 00:05:36,240
And you can tell me

140
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:39,250
all about your first full day back on the job.

141
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:42,250
It's a deal!
